Z||000037||TwisT||03-24-2000||08:41 AM||||Ahhhhhhh...  ain't those pictures cute???  lol once again!<P>I'm sorry,  but I have to confess I haven't much respect for the 'rice crowd' and their whiz-bangin' street contraptions.  I DO however have MUCH respect with those dedicated import tuners who drive TRUE performance cars,  such as the almighty Twin Turbo Nissan Z,  Acura NSX and the Toyota Supra.  Imports?  Yes.  Whiz-bangin' 4-cylinder big-tip-wearing and sticker-bound ricers???  NOPE!  Much respect goes to these guys.<P>DOWNSIDE to any import?  ALL THAT DAMN MONEY SPENT JUST TO GET IT TO RUN 14 SECOND QUARTER MILES!!!<P>LOL...  What a riot!  ||||reg||1
Z||000038||Dan86gt3.8||03-24-2000||03:35 PM||||Ya I always hear all the ricers talk about dissapointing V8's.  But not many out there  can, granted a supra and other cars can really tear it up out there.  But usually the guy you see talking about beating V8 muscle is a moron in a sticker charged civic that runs 20 second 1/4 miles.  Or wait maybe they are talking about beating thoose 2.6 mustangs, hey that I believe!  But if you are gona talk crap about your turbo ricers lookt at american turbo cars.  You can buy a grand national or PONTIAC trans am with the 3.8 turbo motor and it can be in the 12's with about 300 in mods, or if you build the engines and go with bigger turbos (yep just like the ricers do) you have an 11-10 second car that is a complete sleeper.  But for the most part, here intexas ricers don't amount to jack crap.  I am sure there are all over so. CAL, but here in the dirty south, repectable ricers are few in far between, except in houston I hear they are everywhere, but anytime you get around a big city they are gona come out of the wood work.  But I do have 1 question, do you ever see them parked in a driveway or really anywhere for that matter?  Everytime I see one its out driving.||||reg||13
